  "description": "- Extending the existing kitchen towards side to rear garden, replacing the existing window  with bi-folding doors and placing 3 skylights  on the extended flat roof portion. (Total added area: 10.92 sqm)\n\n- Replacing the Ground Floor studio's (ex-garage)  existing side window (linear one at a top level) with new windows. \n\n- Erecting a first floor extension on top of the existing studio which had been priorly converted from a garage, by setting back distance from the front and rear elevations' ground floor boundaries. This extension will enable 1 bedroom and 1 bathroom to be added to the usage of the house. (Total added area: 30.94 sqm)\n\n- Conversion of Loft by adding 2 sets of dormer windows and allowing a partial flat roof (which would accomodate solar panels on top for green energy) along with the adjoining of the new pitched roof of first floor extension to the existing pitched roof. Gained space on Loft Floor allows 1 bathroom and a recreational space added to the usage. Along with the dormer windows 1 skylight roof window and 1 small window is proposed to be added to the rear facade. \n\n- The flat roof portion of the new roof will be limited in height to match with the adjacent neighbours’ (54 and 56 St Albans Avenue)’s existing loft conversion’s top level. \n\n\n\n\n",
